.Dd November 18, 2026
.Dt ARCANA-ENROL 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm arcana-enrol
.Nd join this host to a arcana console
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl is
.Op Fl a Ar address ...
.Op Fl f Ar sha256 ...
.Op Fl p Ar port
.Op Fl d Ar directory
.Op Fl n Ar name
.Ar console-url token
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
gets this host a certificate from the arcana console's certificate
authority, so that
.Xr arcana-agent 8
can serve the console over mutual TLS.
It makes an EC P-256 key and a certificate request, sends the request to
.Ar console-url
with the one-time
.Ar token
the console issued for this host, and writes what comes back:
the token,
.Dq arce1_
and base64url of the console's 32-byte secret followed by the SHA-256
of each certificate of the CA this host is to trust, pins that CA.
Before the token is sent,
.Nm
asks
.Ar console-url
for its CA without it, and goes no further unless each of its
certificates is one the token pins: a console other than the one that
made the token is not given it.
Each certificate of the CA that comes back with this host's certificate
must be one of them too, and then
.Nm
writes:
.Pp
.Bl -tag -width "host.key" -compact -offset indent
.It Pa host.key
the private key, mode 0600;
.It Pa host.pem
the certificate, for the name the token was made for;
.It Pa ca.pem
the console's CA, which signs the console's own client certificate.
.El
.Pp
The files go to
.Pa /usr/local/etc/arcana .
The console adds this host to its server list at the same time, as
.Pa tcp://host:port .
Then
.Nm
prints the
.Xr rc.conf 5
lines that run
.Xr arcana-agent 8
with the files, or sets them itself with
.Fl s .
.Pp
The options are:
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl a Ar address
An address
.Xr arcana-agent 8
is to listen on, in the printed or applied flags; may be given more
than once.
The default is every address, over IPv4 and IPv6 both:
.Li 0.0.0.0
and
.Li \&:: .
.It Fl d Ar directory
Write the files there instead of
.Pa /usr/local/etc/arcana .
.It Fl f Ar sha256
A SHA-256 fingerprint of a CA to trust, as
.Ql openssl x509 -noout -fingerprint -sha256
of its
.Pa ca.pem
shows it, with colons or without; may be given more than once.
With a token that carries fingerprints, each
.Fl f
must be one of them, or
.Nm
stops before it sends anything: the fingerprint and the token say
different consoles.
Each certificate of the CA the console sends must be one the token or
.Fl f
names, or
.Nm
sends no token and writes nothing: the CA is what
.Xr arcana-agent 8
is to trust.
.It Fl i
Enrol over plain HTTP: without it a
.Ar console-url
that is not
.Li https://
is refused, for the token and the CA would travel in the clear.
The CA is checked by the token's fingerprints all the same; the token
is not kept from who listens.
A token that carries none (one made by hand) and no
.Fl f
enrol only with
.Fl i ,
the CA taken as it comes.
.It Fl n Ar name
The name in the certificate request.
The console ignores it and names the certificate after the token's host;
the default is this host's name.
.It Fl p Ar port
The port in the flags.
The default is 4310, the port the console will connect to unless the
token was made with another.
.It Fl s
Enable and start
.Xr arcana-agent 8
with
.Xr sysrc 8
and
.Xr service 8 :
it sets
.Va arcana_agent_enable
and the network listeners in
.Va arcana_agent_listen ,
and, with
.Fl d ,
where the files are in
.Va arcana_agent_ca ,
.Va arcana_agent_cert
and
.Va arcana_agent_key .
Without it the command to do so is printed.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
In the console, add a server with
.Dq Enrol a host ,
giving it a name and the host name or address the console reaches it by.
The console shows a command like
.Bd -literal -offset indent
arcana-enrol -s https://console.example arce1_mN3q...
.Ed
.Pp
Run it on the host as root;
.Fl s
has
.Xr arcana-agent 8
enabled and running right away.
Options go before the URL, as
.Xr getopt 3
stops at the first argument.
The token works once and for an hour.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr arcana-agent 8 ,
.Xr arcana-console 8 ,
.Xr arcanactl 8
.Sh SECURITY
The fingerprints the token carries are whole SHA-256s, the same that
.Ql openssl x509 -fingerprint -sha256
shows, so one can be told against the CA by eye.
The console's own HTTPS certificate is checked by
.Xr fetch 3
against the system's trusted CAs.
Over plain HTTP, taken only with
.Fl i ,
or with
.Ev SSL_NO_VERIFY_PEER
set, whoever can read the connection can take the token and have the
certificate issued to a key of their own; the CA this host trusts is
the one the token pins all the same, unless it pins none.
Asking for the CA before the token is sent keeps the token from a
console that is not the token's, but not from one who relays the
connection to the right console unseen: that is what HTTPS is for.
.Pp
Once the console has answered,
.Nm
runs in capability mode
.Pq Xr capsicum 4 :
the answer is parsed and the files are written through the directory
opened beforehand, and nothing else of the system is reachable.
The answer to the first question, the CA alone, is parsed and checked
by a child in capability mode too.
.Xr sysrc 8
and
.Xr service 8
are run by a child forked before that, told to go once the files are
in place.
